// Greetings: the first thing a pony says when you start talking, before the conversation moves on to
// its topic. One is picked like any opener - among the nodes whose "when:" holds, by weight - so the
// more particular the moment, the higher the weight, and it wins when it fits.
//
// Greetings only speak (and run effects); replies and jumps don't belong here - the topic comes next.
//
// The topic is picked first, and only a greeting with the same "tone:" may open it. Plain topics
// get the plain greetings below; heavy ones (breaking news, comforting grief) are "tone: gentle",
// so they only ever get the gentle greetings at the bottom - never a yawn or a joke.
//
// time_of_day(...) is the pony's own clock: bat ponies live by night, so their "morning" is dusk.
// last_talked(...) is just_now, today, a_while (up to a week), long, or never.
//
// PLACEHOLDER LINES - a scaffold showing the shape; every line here is meant to be rewritten.


// ---- Any pony, by time of day ----

=== morning
start: greeting
when: time_of_day(morning)
{pony}: Morning!
    or: Good morning, {player}.

=== afternoon
start: greeting
when: time_of_day(afternoon)
{pony}: Afternoon!
    or: Oh, hello there.

=== evening
start: greeting
when: time_of_day(evening)
{pony}: Evening, {player}.
    or: Nice evening, isn't it?

=== night
start: greeting
when: time_of_day(night)
{pony}: Bit late to be out, isn't it?
    or: Can't sleep either?


// ---- Personality and time together (one example each - add the rest) ----

=== peppy_morning
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: personality(peppy), time_of_day(morning)
{pony}: Good MORNING! Isn't it just the best day?

=== cranky_morning
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: personality(cranky), time_of_day(morning)
{pony}: Ugh. Too early for talking.

=== lazy_afternoon
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: personality(lazy), time_of_day(afternoon)
{pony}: *yawn* Oh... hey. Nap time's almost over anyway.

=== bookish_night
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: personality(bookish), time_of_day(night)
{pony}: Oh! I lost track of time - I was reading.

=== bat_pony_bedtime
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: species(bat_pony), time_of_day(night)
// A bat pony's "night" is daytime for everyone else.
{pony}: *yawns* Shouldn't you let a pony sleep?


// ---- How well they know you ----

=== stranger
start: greeting
weight: 6
when: last_talked(never)
{pony}: Oh, hello! I don't think we've met.

// PLACEHOLDER. Arriving through someone they love: a friend of yours is family or a friend to them.
=== introduced
start: greeting
weight: 12
when: last_talked(never), mutual_friend
{pony}: Oh! You're {player}, aren't you? {mutual_friend} has told me all about you!

=== close_friend
start: greeting
weight: 4
when: fondness >= high
{pony}: {player}! There you are!

=== wary
start: greeting
weight: 5
when: not trust >= low, not last_talked(never)
{pony}: ...Oh. It's you.


// ---- How recently you talked ----

=== back_again
start: greeting
weight: 8
when: last_talked(just_now)
{pony}: Back again already?
    or: Forget something?

=== long_absence
start: greeting
weight: 6
when: last_talked(long)
{pony}: {player}! Where have you BEEN?


// ---- Their mood ----

=== grieving
start: greeting
weight: 10
when: mood(grief, clear)
{pony}: Oh... hello.

=== joyful
start: greeting
weight: 4
when: mood(joy, clear)
{pony}: Hi hi hi! Oh, I'm so glad to see you!


// ---- Weather ----

=== rain
start: greeting
weight: 3
when: raining, not thundering
{pony}: Come on, get out of the rain!

=== storm
start: greeting
weight: 5
when: thundering
{pony}: Did you hear that thunder?!


// ---- Gentle: before heavy news or comfort ----

=== gentle_hello
start: greeting
tone: gentle
{pony}: Oh... hi, {player}.
    or: Hey. Come here a moment?

=== gentle_stranger
start: greeting
tone: gentle
weight: 6
when: last_talked(never)
{pony}: Hello... you're {player}, aren't you?

=== gentle_friend
start: greeting
tone: gentle
weight: 4
when: fondness >= high
{pony}: *sets everything down* {player}. Hey.
